{"school":{"dbn":"26Q172","name":"Irwin Altman Middle School 172","boro":"Queens","district":"26","district_label":"District 26","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":798,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"81-14 257 STREET, QUEENS, NY 11004","phone":"718-464-5763","website":"www.ms172.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/70523","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Irwin Altman Middle School 172 is located in a \"suburban\" setting in Floral Park, Queens. The school's dedicated, experienced and caring staff use a student-centered middle school philosophy that supports our goal of all students achieving academic excellence in a safe and supportive environment. We honor and celebrate the diversity of our MS 172 community. Our curriculum emphasizes academic exploration and collaborative experiences in the development of critical thinking. Approximately 1/2 of our grade 8 students earn HS credit in science, math, social studies and foreign language. MS 172 is in ongoing partnership with the UA Science Initiative highlighting collaborations with science cultural institutions, with Reel Works to provide students with curriculum-related moving image and filming experiences, with SAYA! (South Asian Youth Action,) in offering a Girls' Leadership Group, with the Ronald McDonald House for community service opportunities, and with the DOE C.H.A.M.P.S. program to provide before and after-school sports. In partnership with the Common Point Queens Beacon, we can provide additional after school and holiday activities. Students at MS 172 have participated in and have received honors in the Games for Change Challenge, the NYS School Music Association competition, and several art and debate competitions.","start_time":"08:00am","end_time":"02:19pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"Q36, Q43, Q46, QM35, QM36, QM5, QM6, QM8, X68","shared_building":"0","neighb